Kind: ablation
Issue: #801
Over: 801-widen-give-back.patch
Takes out: the signals ignored while the lock goes back -- stopped_by() puts INT, TERM and HUP back to their default first again, as before the fix, so the second SIGTERM that systemctl stop sends, once the unit's main process has died on the first, ends the script with the lock held; over the widen, which holds give_back() open a second, every stopped boot must leave it, and harness-lifecycle-check.sh's unitstop say so for run-x86_64.sh while the tools on their own lock pass
Script: scripts/harness-lifecycle-check.sh
Script: --only
Script: unitstop
Expect: lifecycle: unitstop run-x86_64\.sh: .*the lock is STILL THERE

diff --git a/scripts/run-x86_64.sh b/scripts/run-x86_64.sh
index ec9a537b..3065a94f 100755
--- a/scripts/run-x86_64.sh
+++ b/scripts/run-x86_64.sh
@@ -1200,11 +1200,9 @@ give_back() {
 	LOCK_ID=""
 }
 stopped_by() {
-	trap - EXIT
-	trap '' INT TERM HUP
+	trap - EXIT INT TERM HUP
 	give_back
 	echo "run-x86_64.sh: stopped by SIG$1 -- its qemu stopped and the lock given back" >&2
-	trap - INT TERM HUP
 	kill -s "$1" "$$"
 }
 trap give_back EXIT
